{title: O for a Thousand Tongues to Sing}
{artist: Charles Wesley / Carl Gläser}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 23장}
{title_ko: 만 입이 내게 있으면}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: o-for-a-thousand-tongues-to-sing.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]O for a thousand [C]tongues to [G]sing
My [Em]great Re[D]deemer's [G]praise
The [G]glories of my [C]God and [G]King
The [Em]triumphs [D]of His [G]grace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]My gracious Master [C]and my [G]God
As[Em]sist me [D]to pro[G]claim
To [G]spread through all the [C]earth a[G]broad
The [Em]honors [D]of Thy [G]name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Jesus! the name that [C]charms our [G]fears
That [Em]bids our [D]sorrows [G]cease
'Tis [G]music in the [C]sinner's [G]ears
'Tis [Em]life and [D]health and [G]peace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]He breaks the power of [C]canceled [G]sin
He [Em]sets the [D]prisoner [G]free
His [G]blood can make the [C]foulest [G]clean
His [Em]blood a[D]vailed for [G]me
{end_of_verse}
